# Historical basis: Ervand Abrahamian, Iran Between Two Revolutions, ch. 5,
# pp. 250–253, which dates the Sixteenth-Majles election period from July
# 1949; Fakhreddin Azimi, Iran: The Crisis of Democracy, 1941–1953,
# pp. 207–208. All player operations and effects are counterfactual.
title: Election Preparations
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: election_preparations_timer <= 0 and front_formed = 0 and year = 1949 and month >= 5
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; election_preparations_timer = 3

= Election Preparations

[? if month < 7: Preparations are beginning for the election to the Sixteenth
{!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!}. ?]
[? if month >= 7: The election to the Sixteenth
{!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!} is under way. ?]
Candidates and organizations opposed to administrative interference do not
yet possess a common slate, monitoring body, or campaign command.

They can nevertheless coordinate one practical task before scattered
complaints harden into a general election crisis.

- @election_candidates
- @election_observers
- @election_correspondents

@election_candidates
title: Compare prospective candidates
subtitle: Private coordination reduces collisions among constitutional candidates without presenting them as one slate
on-arrival: independent_nationalists_relation += 3; iran_party_relation += 2; public_mandate += 1

Representatives compare constituencies, local connections, and the claims
different candidates intend to make. Some avoid competing directly where
doing so would divide the same limited body of supporters.

The talks improve coordination without producing a national list or binding
any participant to a {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!}
that does not yet exist.

- @post_event: Continue

@election_observers
title: Prepare common observer forms
subtitle: Comparable records strengthen later objections, even though observers cannot compel honest administration
on-arrival: parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += 3; organizational_reach += 2

Lawyers devise a short form recording the place, date, witness, reported act,
and available document. Candidates distribute it where they have trustworthy
contacts and leave unsupported allegations marked as allegations.

The resulting files will be easier to compare. The observers have no power to
certify the election or prevent interference.

- @post_event: Continue

@election_correspondents
title: Concentrate on Tehran and provincial correspondence
subtitle: A wider reporting circuit reveals recurring complaints while leaving candidate coordination unresolved
on-arrival: organizational_reach += 3; press_capacity += 2

Editors and candidates establish regular routes for reports from Tehran and
selected provincial constituencies. Repeated methods become easier to
distinguish from a single local grievance.

The correspondence broadens the coming public case. Candidates still enter
the contest through separate organizations and personal followings.

- @post_event: Continue
